ferry setup

[1/7] bar plugin (ferry.bar: the widget and panels in omarchy-shell)
  will do:
  $ ln -s <tmp>/usr/share/ferry/plugin ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/ferry.bar
  $ omarchy-shell -q shell rescanPlugins
  --- ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json (add the widget to the bar: right, after omarchy.tray)
              "id": "omarchy.tray"
            },
  +         {
  +           "id": "ferry.bar"
  +         },
            {
              "id": "omarchy.keyboard-layout"
  apply? yes (--yes)
  backup: ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json.ferry-bak.1800000000
  done: linked ferry.bar and put the widget on the bar (right, after omarchy.tray)

[2/7] ferryd.service
  ferryd.service is not enabled, not active.
  will do:
  --- ~/.config/systemd/user/ferryd.service (new file)
  + # Written by `ferry setup`; `ferry setup --undo` removes this file (ExecStart is this build's ferryd).
  + # ferry daemon: one keyboard and mouse across Omarchy machines.
  + #
  + # Packaged copy: /usr/lib/systemd/user/ferryd.service. `ferry setup` writes the same file to
  + # ~/.config/systemd/user/ferryd.service for a build without a package, with ExecStart= set to
  + # the ferryd next to the ferry that ran setup.
  + [Unit]
  + Description=ferry daemon: one keyboard and mouse across Omarchy machines
  + PartOf=graphical-session.target
  + After=graphical-session.target
  + StartLimitIntervalSec=0
  + 
  + [Service]
  + Type=notify
  + NotifyAccess=main
  + ExecStart=<tmp>/bin/ferryd
  + Restart=on-failure
  + RestartSec=200ms
  + RestartSteps=5
  + RestartMaxDelaySec=10s
  + WatchdogSec=2s
  + TimeoutStartSec=10s
  + TimeoutStopSec=3s
  + NoNewPrivileges=yes
  + LimitCORE=0
  + UMask=0077
  + SyslogIdentifier=ferryd
  + 
  + [Install]
  + WantedBy=graphical-session.target
  $ systemctl --user daemon-reload
  $ systemctl --user enable --now ferryd
  apply? yes (--yes)
  done: ferryd.service is enabled and started

[3/7] escape bind (SUPER + CTRL + ESCAPE returns input from any capture)
  will do:
  --- ~/.config/hypr/ferry.lua (new file)
  + -- Written by `ferry setup`; `ferry setup --undo` removes this file and its require line.
  + 
  + -- ferry:begin escape-bind
  + -- Escape bind: returns input to this machine even if ferryd hangs.
  + hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ESCAPE", hl.dsp.release_input_capture(), { allow_input_capture = true, description = "ferry: release input capture" })
  + -- ferry:end escape-bind
  --- ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua (append)
  + 
  + -- ferry: loads ferry.lua (`ferry setup --undo` removes this line)
  + require("hypr.ferry")
  apply? yes (--yes)
  backup: ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua.ferry-bak.1800000000
  done: Hyprland loaded it

[4/7] go binds (the go chord and an arrow key move to the machine on that side)
  will do:
  --- ~/.config/hypr/ferry.lua (append)
  + 
  + -- ferry:begin go-binds
  + -- Go binds: move the keyboard and mouse to the machine on that side.
  + hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + LEFT", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("ferry go left"), { description = "ferry: go left" })
  + hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + RIGHT", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("ferry go right"), { description = "ferry: go right" })
  + hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + UP", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("ferry go up"), { description = "ferry: go up" })
  + hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + DOWN", hl.dsp.exec_cmd("ferry go down"), { description = "ferry: go down" })
  + -- ferry:end go-binds
  apply? yes (--yes)
  backup: ~/.config/hypr/ferry.lua.ferry-bak.1800000000
  done: Hyprland loaded it

[5/7] release_pressed_on_close (clients see key-ups when a virtual keyboard dies)
  will do:
  --- ~/.config/hypr/ferry.lua (append)
  + 
  + -- ferry:begin release-pressed-on-close
  + -- Clients see key-ups when a virtual keyboard dies.
  + hl.config({ input = { virtualkeyboard = { release_pressed_on_close = true } } })
  + -- ferry:end release-pressed-on-close
  apply? yes (--yes)
  backup: ~/.config/hypr/ferry.lua.ferry-bak.1800000000.1
  done: Hyprland loaded it

